# which camera the recording is filmed with: "front" or "back". The default is
# front — "default selfie" is the word from the earlier prompt this row's
# camera button carries forward (#p5) — and it is set HERE rather than in
# flip.vars so that unticking this node puts /flip's own default (back) back.
# Device-scoped, exactly as /flip's `facing` was and for /flip's reason: how
# you work is not what you own, and a device write queues no op. Bridged,
# because the page half is where the camera is actually asked for.
camera: String = "front".to_string() (device, last-write, own) js:camera

# the level a NEW post is stamped at, in place of the author's own grade: one
# of /audience's six words, or empty for "same as me". User-scoped, not
# device: which room you are talking to is a decision about you, so it belongs
# to the person and follows them to their other phone (/one-add's `mode` is
# the other kind of setting and stays on its device).
post_level: String = String::new() (user, last-write, own) js:post_level
